#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# dependencies = [
#   "pyyaml>=6.0",
# ]
# ///
"""
Anthive process supervisor

Starts all backend services, multiplexes their output with colored labels,
and auto-restarts any crashed child process.

Subcommands (control plane):
  ant-supervisor                         # run all services (default)
  ant-supervisor --caddy                 # run with Caddy on :8501 (dev)
  ant-supervisor --prod --caddy          # run with Caddy on 127.0.0.1:8500
                                         #   (nginx terminates TLS upstream)
  ant-supervisor restart <name>…         # SIGTERM a running child by name
  ant-supervisor restart all             # SIGTERM every running child
  ant-supervisor status                  # show supervisor + child PIDs

Prod mode (via --prod or ANTHIVE_PROD=1 in the environment):
  - Caddy listens on http://127.0.0.1:8500 (plain HTTP, no TLS).
  - nginx terminates TLS on :443 in front of Caddy and is the
    Authelia auth_request gate.  See config/examples/nginx-vhost.*.conf.example.
  - Caddy still owns ALL anthive path routing (single source of truth).
  - The :8500 → :8501 HTTPS redirect block is disabled (would collide
    with the prod listener on the same port).

The flag is passed to Caddy via four env vars consumed by config/Caddyfile:
  ANTHIVE_LISTEN, ANTHIVE_TLS_SNIPPET, ANTHIVE_AUTH_SNIPPET,
  ANTHIVE_HTTP_REDIRECT_SNIPPET, ANTHIVE_CADDY_BIND.
"""

